# Triangle Terrain Plugin: Version Bump Required

When you modify ANY file under `memories/TriangleTerrainPlugin/src/`, you MUST update `src/Version.luau` BEFORE running `build_rbxmx.py`. The version string is shown in the plugin's dock widget title so the user can immediately see which build is loaded.

## Bump rules (semver)

- **PATCH** (0.0.x): bug fixes, internal refactors, doc/comment changes, no user-visible behavior change
- **MINOR** (0.x.0): new feature, new mode, new UI section, expanded capability, new module
- **MAJOR** (x.0.0): breaking change to data format, removed features, large rewrites

## Workflow

1. Make your code changes.
2. Edit `src/Version.luau`: bump `Version.STRING` and add a one-line entry to the in-file `History` block describing what shipped.
3. Run `python build_rbxmx.py` to write the updated `.rbxmx` to the user's Plugins folder.
4. Tell the user the new version (e.g. "Built v0.4.0 — added X").

If multiple changes are batched in one task, do ONE bump for the combined work — pick the highest applicable level (MINOR > PATCH).
